:Namespace Harness
⍝ Match harness (oracle Phase 3): agents, opening replay, colour-swapped pairs, statistics, opening-set splits.
⍝ (A _Match_ B) openings → per pair, A's points as Black then White; seed Report result → one line of text.
    ⎕IO←0
    eng←#.Othello
    gm←#.Games
    _RA←{b←1⊃⍵ ⋄ s←⍸eng.Moves b ⋄ ⎕RL←1+2147483646|⍺⍺+eng.Key b ⋄ s[?≢s]} ⍝ agent (seed _RA): random move, reproducible from seed and position
    Greedy←{b←1⊃⍵ ⋄ s←⍸eng.Moves b ⋄ s[⊃⍒+/(s eng.Play(≢s)2 64⍴b)[;1;]]} ⍝ agent: most discs after the move, lowest square on ties
    Replay←{ ⍝ game after opening squares ⍵ from game ⍺ (default: start, Black to move); colour toggles on placements and passes
        ⍺←0 eng.start ⋄ 0=≢⍵:⍺ ⋄ c b←⍺
        eng.Terminal b:'opening runs past the end of the game'⎕SIGNAL 11
        ~∨/eng.Moves b:(~c)(⊖b)∇⍵
        (⊃⍵)∊⍸eng.Moves b:(~c)((⊃⍵)eng.Play b)∇1↓⍵
        'illegal opening move'⎕SIGNAL 11
    }
    Done←{eng.Terminal 1⊃⍵:⍵ ⋄ 'agent stopped with legal moves'⎕SIGNAL 11} ⍝ a match game must be played to the end
    _Duel_←{ ⍝ agent ⍺⍺ plays Black, ⍵⍵ White, from game ⍵ → finished game
        ⊃⍵:Done(⍵⍵ gm._Game_ ⍺⍺)⍵
        Done(⍺⍺ gm._Game_ ⍵⍵)⍵
    }
    Pts←{0.5×1+×gm.Result ⍵} ⍝ Black's points for finished game ⍵: win 1, draw ½, loss 0
    _Pair_←{g←Replay ⍵ ⋄ (Pts(⍺⍺ _Duel_ ⍵⍵)g),1-Pts(⍵⍵ _Duel_ ⍺⍺)g} ⍝ A ≡ ⍺⍺'s points from opening ⍵ as Black, then as White
    _Match_←{↑(⍺⍺ _Pair_ ⍵⍵)¨↓⍵} ⍝ agents ⍺⍺ (A) and ⍵⍵ (B) over openings ⍵ (one per row) → per pair: A's points in its two games
    Boot←{ ⍝ seed ⍺; pair scores ⍵ → mean low high informative (oracle stats policy); ⍬ if no pairs
        n←≢⍵ ⋄ n=0:⍬
        m←n÷⍨+/⍵ ⋄ v←n÷⍨+/2*⍨⍵-m
        (n<10)∨v=0:m,(0⌈1⌊m+¯1 1×0.5*⍨(⍟40)÷2×n),0  ⍝ Hoeffding: uninformative
        ⎕RL←⍺ ⋄ r←{⍵[⍋⍵]}n÷⍨+/⍵[?10000 n⍴n]
        m,r[⌊0.5+9999×0.025 0.975],1  ⍝ percentile pair bootstrap, 10 000 resamples
    }
    Elo←{400×10⍟⍵÷1-⍵} ⍝ rating difference for expected score ⍵
    Report←{ ⍝ seed ⍺; _Match_ result ⍵ → text: pairs, W/D/L, mean pair score with interval, Elo range when both ends are inside (0,1)
        p←2÷⍨+/⍵ ⋄ w d l←+/1 0.5 0∘.=,⍵ ⋄ b←⍺ Boot p
        0=≢b:'insufficient data'
        m lo hi i←b ⋄ J←{1↓∊⍺,¨⍵}                                    ⍝ join texts ⍵ with ⍺
        e←{(lo>0)∧hi<1:'  Elo [',(','J 1⍕¨Elo lo hi),']' ⋄ ''}0
        'pairs ',(⍕≢p),'  W/D/L ',('/'J⍕¨w d l),'  score ',(3⍕m),' [',(','J 3⍕¨lo hi),'] ',(i⊃'uninformative' 'bootstrap'),e
    }
    Tr←{s←⍴⍵ ⋄ s⍴(⌽∘⍉⍣(4|⍺))∘(⍉⍣(⍺≥4))⍤2⊢⍵⍴⍨8 8,⍨¯1↓s} ⍝ D4 element ⍺∊⍳8 applied to board or 64-vector ⍵
    Canon←{b←⍵ ⋄ ⌊/{eng.Key ⍵ Tr b}¨⍳8} ⍝ canonical D4 key of board ⍵: least key over its 8 symmetries
    Splits←{ ⍝ opening sets ⍵ (one matrix each) → (per set: openings, duplicate lines, plies, ply-4 groups, first 20 in distinct groups) (groups shared by two sets)
        G←{Canon 1⊃Replay 4↑⍵} ⋄ gk←{G¨↓⍵}¨⍵
        s←↑{n←≢⍵ ⋄ n,(n-≢∪↓⍵),⊢/⍴⍵}¨⍵
        (s,(≢¨∪¨gk),⍪{20=≢∪20↑⍵}¨gk)(+/,(∘.<⍨⍳≢gk)×∘.{≢⍺∩⍵}⍨∪¨gk)
    }
    Data←{ ⍝ table ⍵ from data.dcf next to the file this namespace was fixed from; component 1 is a namespace of tables
        t←((⊃1⎕NPARTS 3⊃5179⌶⍕⎕THIS),'data.dcf')⎕FSTIE 0
        n←⎕FREAD t 1 ⋄ z←⎕FUNTIE t ⋄ n⍎⍵
    }
:EndNamespace
